      "message": "While this works, it sets the first solid color from the paint to a variable called `outColor_0` (rather than `initialColor` as we had before). Is that sufficiently clear? \n\nIf not, we have some other options that we can consider:\n- Handle the solid shader block first and independently (outside of `emit_glue_code_for_entry`)\n- Add an optional argument on to emit_glue_code_for_entry that allows the caller to override the default naming convention of \"outColor_%d\" (where `d` \u003d the entry index).\n\nLet me know what you think.",
